      "node_type": "kg",
      "content": "Vaikom Padmanabha Pillai (1767–1809) was a militia leader and military officer of the Kingdom of Travancore (now roughly the Indian state of Kerala). In 1808 he led an uprising against British control in Travancore. He was captured in 1809 and hanged for his role in the rebellion.",
